{"id":"bashemath","name":"Bashemath","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:bashemath"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Bashemath","text":"Sweet-smelling. (1.) The daughter of Ishmael, the last of Esau’s three wives (Gen. 36:3, 4, 13), from whose son Reuel four tribes of the Edomites sprung. She is also called Mahalath (Gen. 28:9). It is noticeable that Esau’s three wives receive different names in the genealogical table of the Edomites (Gen. 36) from those given to them in the history (Gen. 26:34; 28:9). (2.) A daughter of Solomon, and wife of Ahimaaz, one of his officers (1 Kings 4:15)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1315","lemma":"בׇּשְׂמַת","xlit":"Bosmath","gloss":"Bosmath, the name of a wife of Esau, and of a daughter of Solomon","kjv":"Bashemath, Basmath","count":6,"share":1},{"strong":"H802","lemma":"אִשָּׁה","xlit":"ʼishshâh","gloss":"a woman","kjv":"ess, each, every, female","count":4,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":4,"share":0.67}],"verses":["Gen.26.34","Gen.36.3","Gen.36.4","Gen.36.10","Gen.36.13","Gen.36.17"],"related":[{"id":"reuel","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.267,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"eliphaz","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.158,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"abihail","type":"lexical","strong":"H802","why":"both lead with אִשָּׁה (H802)"},{"id":"abijah","type":"lexical","strong":"H802","why":"both lead with אִשָּׁה (H802)"},{"id":"adah","type":"lexical","strong":"H802","why":"both lead with אִשָּׁה (H802)"},{"id":"adultery","type":"lexical","strong":"H802","why":"both lead with אִשָּׁה (H802)"},{"id":"ahinoam","type":"lexical","strong":"H802","why":"both lead with אִשָּׁה (H802)"},{"id":"alliance-and-society-with-the-enemies-of-god","type":"lexical","strong":"H802","why":"both lead with אִשָּׁה (H802)"}],"works":[]}
